 is a contested roll. If they are not present it is far easier for the power to succeed. Having them out of the room isn't about them noticing or asking questions but the fact that they reduce the likely hood of success with their presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T02:52:07-07:00","id":886056,"title":"","content":"My understanding was that this only works to duplicate 'powers'. Inherent abilities (Vampire/Werewolf regen, werewolf shapeshifting, Geist resurrection, anything that's not bought as a 'power') are off limits.<br /> <br /> For mage spells, I'd only allow it to replicate exact spells that are observed. And no, Paradox wouldn't apply. You're coercing the universe into duplicating a magical effect, not drawing down the Supernal yourself.<br /> <br /> Edit: A quick read through proves me wrong on the first point. Inherent abilities are totally fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-09-2016, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}